findings.comment:
750.800e -  The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled with grease, splash, and/or debris:
A) (R) grill - 1. sides & 2. underneath surfaces; 
B) (R)  tall 2 door freezer - 1. wheels, 2. underneath surfaces, 3. gaskets and hinges inside doors, & 4. side next to fryers;
C) (R) small fan sitting in order window (dust);
D) table holding grill;
E) table holding hot holding units and canned foods;
F) reach-in cooler - 1. side next to grill & 2. underneath surfaces;  and
G) fryers - 1. sides & 2. underneath surfaces.

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.

750.800b - The following food contact surfaces were soiled with mold, food debris, and/or general buildup:
A) (R) lower edge of ice machine drip guard;
B) (R) soda gun holder at bar;
C) (R) pizza oven;
D) hood filters over cooking equipment in kitchen; and
E) bowls and tongs left with breading and wing sauce from the previous evening.
Clean and sanitize food contact surfaces between uses/as needed to prevent cross contamination and eliminate buildup of debris.
**In-use utensils and equipment (i.e. knives, cutting boards, tongs, breading and wing sauce bowls, etc.) must be switched out and go through ware washing up to every 4hrs.**

750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled with grease, splash, and/or debris:
A) (R) tall 2 door freezer - 1. inner surfaces of doors, 2. along gaskets, 3. hinges, 4. wheels, 5. underneath surfaces, & 6. side of freezer next to fryers;
B) (R) wall mounted storage rack on the right side of tall 2 door freezer; 
C) (R) fryers - 1. general surfaces inside around mechanicals, 2. sides, 3. legs, & 4. underneath surfaces (grease hanging from bottom underneath); 
D) small freezer - 1. wheels & 2. underneath surfaces;
E) grill - 1. sides, 2. underneath surfaces, & 3. waste pan;
F) table holding grill;
G) table holding food warmers and unopened dressings; and
H) shelf holding juice, olives, and mixers inside bar cooler.
Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.
